---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — WorthIt"
  description="How WorthIt handles photos, accounts, scan history, and the providers used to check shelf prices."
>
  <main class="legal-page" id="main">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">WORTHIT</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">
        Effective date: May 10, 2026 · <a href="/">WorthIt home</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
      </p>
      <div class="legal-shell">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy describes how WorthIt (“we,” “us,” or “our”) handles information when you use the WorthIt
          mobile app and related services (the “Service”). WorthIt is operated by an independent developer. A formal
          legal entity name and mailing address may be added when incorporated.
        </p>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
          WorthIt helps you evaluate products using photos, barcodes, and text you submit. Scan history is stored on
          your device unless you later use features that sync elsewhere. Cloud analysis, when enabled, sends your
          inputs to our backend and to AI and lookup providers to produce results. We use Supabase for sign-in and
          operational data such as usage limits when that is configured. We do not sell your personal information.
        </p>
        <h2>Information you provide</h2>
        <p>
          If you create an account, our authentication provider may process your email address, password (hashed by the
          provider), and any profile metadata you add. You may also submit images (for example product or price-tag
          photos), barcode values, and typed text (for example product names or notes) for analysis.
        </p>
        <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
        <p>
          When cloud analysis is enabled, we may store usage counts and plan or tier data tied to your account to
          enforce daily limits. If we add analytics or crash reporting, we will update this Policy to name those tools
          and what they collect.
        </p>
        <h2>On your device</h2>
        <p>
          The app saves your analysis results and related data locally. When you are signed in, scan history (including
          saved-for-later and purchased markers, and location captured for a scan when you allow it) may sync to your
          account so it can be restored on another device. You can clear saved activity from Settings on this device;
          signed-in users may also remove synced copies from the cloud when clearing.
        </p>
        <h2>How we use information</h2>
        <p>
          We use it to run and improve the Service, authenticate accounts, enforce limits and security, generate product
          and price-related insights, and show links to third-party retailers. We may use it to comply with law and
          protect rights and safety. Third-party AI providers (for example Google Gemini) apply their own terms; check
          their documentation for whether your content may be used to improve their models.
        </p>
        <h2>Cloud analysis</h2>
        <p>
          When enabled and you are signed in (or when a custom analysis endpoint is configured), your image (if any),
          text query, mode (for example Save or Flip), and approximate location (when you grant permission) may be sent
          to our backend (for example Supabase Edge Functions). Our backend may call Google Gemini for interpretation.
          For barcode-only lookups, we may send the barcode to Open Food Facts (or similar databases) with minimal
          technical headers required by that service. Results are returned to your app. Server or provider logs may
          temporarily retain related metadata. Signed-in scan history may also store structured fields such as product
          name, prices you confirm, store context, and location metadata for your account.
        </p>
        <h2>Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          Third parties we rely on may include Supabase (authentication, database, serverless functions), Google (Gemini
          API), Open Food Facts (barcode product data), and our cloud hosting provider. Each has its own privacy policy.
        </p>
        <h2>Retailer links</h2>
        <p>
          The Service may open third-party sites (for example Amazon, Walmart, Target, Kroger, or eBay) in your browser.
          Those sites are independent and have their own practices. Some links may include affiliate parameters; see our
          <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> for Amazon Associates and similar disclosures.
        </p>
        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          On-device history remains until you delete it or remove the app. Account and quota data are kept while your
          account is active and as needed for security and legal compliance. Log retention follows our hosting
          provider’s practices unless law requires otherwise.
        </p>
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>We use reasonable measures to protect information. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure.</p>
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your region). We do not knowingly
          collect personal information from children.
        </p>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or export personal information, or
          to object to certain processing. Contact <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> for requests.
        </p>
        <h2>International users</h2>
        <p>
          Information may be processed in the United States or other countries where we or our providers operate. Those
          countries may have different data protection laws.
        </p>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Policy and will adjust the effective date. Material changes may be communicated as required
          by law. This page is published at https://isitworthit.io/privacy.
        </p>
        <p>This Policy is provided for transparency and is not legal advice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
